# SnackPortal2 — build context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.1 GB, because `backend/.venv` alone is ~871 MB. The
# daemon receives the whole context before the first instruction runs, so the cost is paid on
# every build whether or not a layer uses the files — and on this repository it was large
# enough to take the Docker Desktop WSL engine down mid-build (0xc00000fd) rather than merely
# make the build slow.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs named directories rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing below could reach
# the image in any case. This file is about what crosses the wire, not about what lands.

# Virtual environments — the single largest offender.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches. Machine-local, never reproducible, never wanted in an image.
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# setuptools build artifacts. `pip install .[dev]` leaves these in-tree; a stale copy inside
# the image would shadow the freshly installed package.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Tests are not installed into the runtime image. They run on the host and in CI, against the
# source tree, and shipping them would put the live-PostgreSQL harness inside a service image.
tests/

# Local operator tooling and documentation — not runtime.
tools/
migrations/README.md

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
